 "note": "TEST_EXISTING v3 target (public-test-case-existing-v3): 10 exported functions from 6 permissive repos outside lm-corpus (repo and module sha checked against ext-manifest 8458eac6 + ext-corpus.json), each called by an existing test file at the pinned commit (HEAD of the clone) that builds new Date(...) values, where v1 and v2 refuse the function (test_target_signature: Date in the signature or in a followed sibling type) and v3 accepts it on the pinned module text, following relative imports only through the pinned sibling fixtures (4 examples need a sibling). Method: a commit-history scan of the 411 permissive TypeScript repos used for M85 found no test-only commit that fits; the HEAD scan of those 411 repos plus 326 permissive non-fork TypeScript repos found by GitHub repository search (date, calendar, scheduling, timezone and similar topics; MIT/Apache-2.0/BSD-3-Clause/ISC; over 20 stars; not in the corpus) found 16 candidates (at most 3 per repo). Dropped: facioquo/stock-charts toFinancialDataPoint and loadStaticQuotes (the pre-push core-text check matched shingles in their fixtures), CALLE-AI/awesome-phone-call-agents isQuietHour and Kesin11/actions-timeline parseLogBlocks (no Date in the signature itself), callumalpass/tasknotes isEventInRange (license not classified as permissive), pedrofuentes/stream-deck-ical sortEventsByStartTime (an email address in the module). Peace's public repos were checked first (see peace): both have fitting functions (the scan stops at 3 per repo), but both repos are in the corpus manifest, so they are recorded and not counted.",
